MatchSpec.description:
How a rule classifies a field as sensitive. Any combination is allowed;
a field matches the rule if *any* configured criterion matches (name
pattern OR value detector OR explicit field name).

anyOf.description:
Configuration for the MongoDB sink connector.

# Example

```
use faucet_sink_mongodb::MongoSinkConfig;

let config = MongoSinkConfig::new(
    "mongodb://localhost:27017",
    "my_database",
    "my_collection",
)
.with_batch_size(1000);
```

batch_size.description:
Rows per load unit. For `insert`, the per-statement multi-row chunk size;
for `copy`, the number of rows per staged S3 object. Defaults to
[`DEFAULT_BATCH_SIZE`]. `0` = one unit for the whole page.
